        "original_id": "911c024c-f6a1-5344-a3fd-a9a6ef3a2c44",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Diamond White, Alice Walker, Sarah Hyland\n- Groups: Boyce Avenue, Fifth Harmony\n- Works: The Color Purple, The Lion Guard, The Haunted Hathaways, Sofia the First, Phineas and Ferb\n- Topics: singing, acting, voice acting, collaborations\n\nFacts:\n- Alice Walker wrote The Color Purple, a 1982 epistolary novel that won the 1983 Pulitzer Prize for Fiction and the National Book Award for Fiction.\n- Diamond White was born on January 1, 1999, and she is an American singer, actress, and voice actress.\n- In 2007, at age 8, Diamond White starred in a Chicago-based production of The Color Purple that also toured nationally.\n- Diamond White voiced Fuli on the Disney Junior series The Lion Guard.\n- Diamond White had cameo appearances on The Haunted Hathaways and Sofia the First, and she had a recurring role on Phineas and Ferb.\n- Boyce Avenue collaborated with YouTube artists including Hannah Trigwell, Kina Grannis, Tiffany Alvord, Megan Nicole, Alex Goot, Megan and Liz, David Choi, Tyler Ward, Savannah Outen, Cobus Potgieter, John Robby Deleon, and DeStorm Power.\n- Boyce Avenue also collaborated with The X Factor season two finalists Fifth Harmony, Bea Miller, Diamond White, and Carly Rose Sonenclar, as well as actress Sarah Hyland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
