        "text": "Page: Diamond White (singer). Sentence: Diamond White (born January 1, 1999) is an American singer, actress and voice actress who, in 2007 at the age of 8, starred in a Chicago-based production of \"The Color Purple\" that also toured nationally.\nPage: Diamond White (singer). Sentence: She voices Frankie Greene in \",\" Fuli on the Disney Junior series \"The Lion Guard,\" and has had cameo appearances on \"The Haunted Hathaways\" and \"Sofia the First\" and a recurring role on \"Phineas and Ferb.\"\nPage: The Color Purple. Sentence: The Color Purple is a 1982 epistolary novel by American author Alice Walker that won the 1983 Pulitzer Prize for Fiction and the National Book Award for Fiction.\nPage: Boyce Avenue. Sentence: Boyce Avenue has also collaborated with other YouTube artists such as Hannah Trigwell, Kina Grannis, Tiffany Alvord, Megan Nicole, Alex Goot, Megan and Liz, David Choi, Tyler Ward, Savannah Outen, Cobus Potgieter, John Robby Deleon and DeStorm Power and \"The X Factor\" season two finalists Fifth Harmony, Bea Miller, Diamond White, Carly Rose Sonenclar, and also actress Sarah Hyland.",
